<p>
  Now that we have the cardinalities inside the categories labeled, we will label the portion of the diagram outside the circles.
64 people were surveyed, so, <m> 64 - 3 - 42 - 7 = 12</m>. Therefore we label the portion outside the circles (Region IV) with 12.
</p>

<figure>
  <caption>Definitions of Venn Diagrams Notations</caption>
  <image xml:id="venn-ex-egg-apple-sol-05" width="80%">
      <description>Example: Survey | 2 categories | Overlapping ``or''</description>
      <latex-image>
